# CODEOWNERS -- who must review a change before it can land.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# A required-review branch rule counts ANY approval. This file makes the
# approval come from someone who actually owns the area, so a backend change
# cannot be merged by a frontend-only review (and vice versa) -- the exact
# class of mistake that produces a contract drift between the API and the
# Flutter apps.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, so the most specific rules are listed last.
#
# NOTE: replace `@Akasharyan47` with every maintainer handle that should be
# able to approve. A handle that does not exist on this repository makes
# GitHub ignore the rule silently, so verify with
# https://github.com/Akasharyan47/hyperlocal_app/settings/access

# ── Defaults: anything not matched below needs the owner ───────────────────
*                               @Akasharyan47

# ── Release plumbing: only the owner may change what ships ─────────────────
/.github/workflows/             @Akasharyan47
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @Akasharyan47
/scripts/ci/                    @Akasharyan47
/scripts/security/              @Akasharyan47
/infrastructure/                @Akasharyan47
/docs/deployment/               @Akasharyan47

# ── The API contract: backend and every client depend on it ────────────────
# Changing this file without regenerating it (scripts/ci/refresh_api_contract.py)
# blocks the staging deploy, so it gets an explicit owner.
/packages/api_contracts/        @Akasharyan47

# ── Backend ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/backend/                       @Akasharyan47

# ── Flutter clients ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/apps/                          @Akasharyan47
/packages/shared_models/        @Akasharyan47
